IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-interests`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 4, Division 4 -- Substantial shareholdings (ss 79 to 92). Layer 1, part agent sgj.
-- Source file lines 9882-10294. The text is a rendering of the Act, not the official text.
--
-- HOW IT IS MODELLED. One person and one company at a time. A decision function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the
-- text saying no in its own words, NOTHING is "the text does not say"; every branch that answers no or not-covered says why in a comment.
-- Whether a person has an interest in a share is s 7's (sg-interests.l4): s 81(1)(a) calls `s 7 the person has an interest in the shares`
-- with the purpose Division 4 of Part 4. Periods are counted by sg-periods only. "Business day" counts need the public holidays as a list.
-- The clock of every #TRACE of ss 82, 83 and 84 counts business days after the event that starts the duty; ss 86 and 88 count calendar days.
-- Taken as facts (not decided here): whether a body is a company for this Division is s 79(2)'s function below; whether a share is a
-- voting share is s 4(1)'s (the keel's `s 4(1) "voting share"`); who is "an officer in default" is not defined in the ranges read.

§ `Section 79: application and interpretation of Division`

-- s 79(1): the section has effect for the purposes of the Division only.
-- src:9886 | 79.—(1) This section has effect for the purposes of this Division but
-- src:9887 | does not affect the operation of any other provision of this Act.
@ref s 79(1) (src:9886-9887)
GIVEN `the provision is a provision of Division 4 of Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(1) section 79 has effect for the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision is a provision of Division 4 of Part 4`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the operation of any other provision of this Act"

-- s 79(2): what "a company" is, for the purposes of this Division. Paragraph (a) is shown deleted by Act 2 of 2009, and the paragraphs are not closed with "only",
-- so a body that is declared by neither (b) nor (c) is "not covered" (fork F-j79-1: the other reading is that every company under the Act is still one).
-- src:9889 | (2) A reference to a company is a reference —
-- src:9891 | (a) [Deleted by Act 2 of 2009]
-- src:9893 | (b) to a body corporate, being a body incorporated in
-- src:9894 | Singapore, that is for the time being declared by the
-- src:9895 | Minister, by notification in the Gazette, to be a company
-- src:9896 | for the purposes of this Division; or
-- src:9898 | (c) to a body, not being a body corporate formed in Singapore,
-- src:9899 | that is for the time being declared by the Minister, by
-- src:9900 | notification in the Gazette, to be a company for the
-- src:9901 | purposes of this Division.
@ref s 79(2) (src:9889-9901)
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate incorporated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a body that is not a body corporate formed in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has declared the body, by notification in the Gazette, to be a company for the purposes of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(2) the body is a company for the purposes of this Division` MEANS
    IF    `the Minister has declared the body, by notification in the Gazette, to be a company for the purposes of this Division`
      AND (`the body is a body corporate incorporated in Singapore` OR `the body is a body that is not a body corporate formed in Singapore`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "A reference to a company is a reference — (a) [Deleted by Act 2 of 2009]; (b) ...; or (c) ..." does not say "only", and paragraph (a) is deleted

-- s 79(3): an interest in stock is deemed to be an interest in an issued share.
-- src:9905 | (3) In relation to a company the whole or a portion of the share
-- src:9906 | capital of which consists of stock, an interest of a person in any such
-- src:9907 | stock is deemed to be an interest in an issued share in the company
-- src:9908 | having attached to it the same rights as are attached to that stock.
@ref s 79(3) (src:9905-9908)
GIVEN `the company's share capital consists in whole or in part of stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest is an interest of a person in that stock` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(3) the interest in the stock is deemed to be an interest in an issued share in the company` MEANS
    IF `the company's share capital consists in whole or in part of stock` AND `the interest is an interest of a person in that stock`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming is "In relation to a company the whole or a portion of the share capital of which consists of stock"; outside it the subsection is silent

-- s 79(4): "voting share" in s 4(1) refers to a body corporate and includes a body referred to in s 79(2)(c).
-- src:9910 | (4) A reference in the definition of “voting share” in section 4(1) to
-- src:9911 | a body corporate includes a reference to a body referred to in
-- src:9912 | subsection (2)(c).
@ref s 79(4) (src:9910-9912)
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a body referred to in subsection (2)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79(4) the body is within a reference to a body corporate in the definition of "voting share"` MEANS
    IF `the body is a body corporate` OR `the body is a body referred to in subsection (2)(c)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to a body referred to in subsection (2)(c)" -- an open extension, so another body is not covered

§ `Section 80: persons obliged to comply with Division`

-- s 80(1): the obligation extends to all natural persons (resident or not, citizens or not) and all bodies corporate (incorporated or carrying on business in Singapore or not).
-- src:9919 | 80.—(1) The obligation to comply with this Division extends to all
-- src:9920 | natural persons, whether resident in Singapore or not and whether
-- src:9921 | citizens of Singapore or not, and to all bodies corporate, whether
-- src:9922 | incorporated or carrying on business in Singapore or not.
@ref s 80(1) (src:9919-9922)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(1) the obligation to comply with this Division extends to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a natural person` OR `the person is a body corporate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "extends to all natural persons ... and to all bodies corporate" does not say "only"; another kind of person is not covered

-- s 80(2): the Division extends to acts done or omitted outside Singapore.
-- src:9924 | (2) This Division extends to acts done or omitted to be done outside
-- src:9925 | Singapore.
@ref s 80(2) (src:9924-9925)
GIVEN `the act or omission was done or omitted to be done outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(2) this Division extends to the act or omission` MEANS
    IF `the act or omission was done or omitted to be done outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection extends the Division outside Singapore and says nothing of an act inside it

-- s 80(3): the Minister may by order in the Gazette exempt any person or class from all or any of the provisions, subject to the prescribed terms or conditions.
-- src:9927 | (3) The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, exempt any person or
-- src:9928 | any class of persons from all or any of the provisions of this Division,
-- src:9929 | subject to such terms or conditions as may be prescribed.
@ref s 80(3) (src:9927-9929)
GIVEN `the Minister has by order in the Gazette exempted the person, or a class of persons that includes the person, from the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the terms or conditions prescribed for the exemption are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80(3) the person is exempt from the provision of this Division` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has by order in the Gazette exempted the person, or a class of persons that includes the person, from the provision` AND `the terms or conditions prescribed for the exemption are met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the exemption is by Ministerial order "subject to such terms or conditions as may be prescribed"; with no order, or terms unmet, the text does not say

§ `Section 81: substantial shareholdings and substantial shareholders`

-- s 81(4) first: "voting shares" exclude treasury shares, in s 81 and s 83.
-- src:9958 | (4) In this section and section 83, “voting shares” exclude treasury
-- src:9959 | shares.
@ref s 81(4) (src:9958-9959)
GIVEN `the share is a treasury share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81(4) the share is a voting share for the purposes of section 81 and section 83` MEANS
    IF `the share is a treasury share`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section and section 83, “voting shares” exclude treasury shares"
    ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says nothing of a share that is not a treasury share; s 4(1) "voting share" decides

-- s 81(1)(a): "the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares in the company", the interest being s 7's, for the purposes of this Division.
-- src:9936 | (a) the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting
-- src:9937 | shares in the company; and
@ref s 81(1)(a) (src:9936-9937)
GIVEN `the shares are voting shares as section 4(1) defines the term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      facts IS A `s 7 interest facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81(1)(a) the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares in the company` MEANS
    IF    `the shares are voting shares as section 4(1) defines the term`
      AND (NOT (`s 81(4) the share is a voting share for the purposes of section 81 and section 83` `the shares are treasury shares` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
      AND (`s 7 the person has an interest in the shares` `s 7(1) Division 4 of Part 4` facts EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has a substantial shareholding in a company if (a) the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting shares in the company" -- a condition the text introduces with "if" (marginal reading (a))

-- s 81(1)(b): "the total votes attached to that share, or those shares, is not less than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the company".
-- Written without a division: 100 times the votes is at least 5 times the total.
-- src:9939 | (b) the total votes attached to that share, or those shares, is not
-- src:9940 | less than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting
-- src:9941 | shares in the company.
@ref s 81(1)(b) (src:9939-9941)
GIVEN `the total votes attached to the shares in which the person has an interest` IS A NUMBER
      `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the company` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81(1)(b) the votes are not less than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the company` MEANS
    IF (`the total votes attached to the shares in which the person has an interest` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (`the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the company` TIMES 5)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if ... (b) the total votes attached to that share, or those shares, is not less than 5%" -- a condition introduced with "if"

-- s 81(1): a substantial shareholding in a company, one class of shares or none.
-- src:9933 | 81.—(1) For the purposes of this Division, a person has a
-- src:9934 | substantial shareholding in a company if —
-- src:9936 | (a) the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting
-- src:9937 | shares in the company; and
-- src:9939 | (b) the total votes attached to that share, or those shares, is not
-- src:9940 | less than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting
-- src:9941 | shares in the company.
@ref s 81(1) (src:9933-9941)
GIVEN `the body is a company for the purposes of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (a) of subsection (1) holds` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `limb (b) of subsection (1) holds` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81(1) the person has a substantial shareholding in the company` MEANS
    IF `the body is a company for the purposes of this Division` AND (`limb (a) of subsection (1) holds` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`limb (b) of subsection (1) holds` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has a substantial shareholding in a company if (a) ...; and (b) ..." -- a condition introduced with "if" (marginal reading (a))

-- s 81(2): where the share capital is divided into 2 or more classes: interest in voting shares included in one of those classes, with 5% of the votes of that class.
-- src:9943 | (2) For the purposes of this Division, a person has a substantial
-- src:9944 | shareholding in a company, being a company the share capital of
-- src:9945 | which is divided into 2 or more classes of shares, if —
-- src:9947 | (a) the person has an interest or interests in one or more voting
-- src:9948 | shares included in one of those classes; and
-- src:9950 | (b) the total votes attached to that share, or those shares, is not
-- src:9951 | less than 5% of the total votes attached to all the voting
-- src:9952 | shares included in that class.
@ref s 81(2) (src:9943-9952)
GIVEN `the body is a company for the purposes of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share capital of the company is divided into 2 or more classes of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (a) of subsection (2) holds` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the total votes attached to the shares in which the person has an interest` IS A NUMBER
      `the total votes attached to all the voting shares included in that class` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81(2) the person has a substantial shareholding in the company, the share capital of which is divided into 2 or more classes` MEANS
    IF    `the body is a company for the purposes of this Division`
      AND `the share capital of the company is divided into 2 or more classes of shares`
      AND (`limb (a) of subsection (2) holds` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
      AND ((`the total votes attached to the shares in which the person has an interest` TIMES 100) AT LEAST (`the total votes attached to all the voting shares included in that class` TIMES 5))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person has a substantial shareholding in a company, being a company the share capital of which is divided into 2 or more classes of shares, if (a) ...; and (b) ..." -- a condition introduced with "if" (marginal reading (a))

-- s 81(3): a person who has a substantial shareholding is a substantial shareholder.
-- The text gives one direction ("is") and does not say "only": a person with neither a (1) nor a (2) shareholding is not covered (fork F-j81-1).
-- src:9954 | (3) For the purposes of this Division, a person who has a substantial
-- src:9955 | shareholding in a company is a substantial shareholder in that
-- src:9956 | company.
@ref s 81(3) (src:9954-9956)
GIVEN `the person has a substantial shareholding in the company under subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has a substantial shareholding in the company under subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81(3) the person is a substantial shareholder in the company` MEANS
    IF `the person has a substantial shareholding in the company under subsection (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the person has a substantial shareholding in the company under subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "a person who has a substantial shareholding in a company is a substantial shareholder in that company" -- one direction, no "means" and no "only"

§ `Section 82: substantial shareholder to notify company of interests`

DECLARE `s 82 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 82(1) give written notice to the company of the person's interests`

-- s 82(1): the content of the notice.
-- src:9966 | 82.—(1) A person who is a substantial shareholder in a company
-- src:9967 | must give written notice to the company stating the person’s name
-- src:9968 | and address and full particulars (including, unless the interest or
-- src:9969 | interests cannot be related to a particular share or shares, the name of
-- src:9970 | the person who is registered as the holder) of the voting shares in the
-- src:9971 | company in which the person has an interest or interests and full
-- src:9972 | particulars of each such interest and of the circumstances by reason of
-- src:9973 | which the person has that interest.
@ref s 82(1) (src:9966-9973)
GIVEN `the person is a substantial shareholder in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in writing and is given to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the person's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states full particulars of the voting shares in the company in which the person has an interest or interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interest or interests cannot be related to a particular share or shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the name of the person who is registered as the holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states full particulars of each such interest and of the circumstances by reason of which the person has that interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82(1) the notice is the notice the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a substantial shareholder in the company`
      AND `the notice is in writing and is given to the company`
      AND `the notice states the person's name and address`
      AND `the notice states full particulars of the voting shares in the company in which the person has an interest or interests`
      AND (`the interest or interests cannot be related to a particular share or shares` OR `the notice states the name of the person who is registered as the holder`)
      AND `the notice states full particulars of each such interest and of the circumstances by reason of which the person has that interest`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who is a substantial shareholder in a company must give written notice to the company stating ..." -- a duty: the provision's own question

-- s 82(2): when the notice must be given.
-- src:9975 | (2) The notice must be given —
-- src:9977 | (a) if the person was a substantial shareholder on 1 October
-- src:9978 | 1971 — within one month after that date; or
-- src:9980 | (b) if the person became a substantial shareholder after that
-- src:9981 | date — within 2 business days after becoming a substantial
-- src:9982 | shareholder.
@ref s 82(2) (src:9975-9982)
GIVEN `the person was a substantial shareholder on 1 October 1971` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person became a substantial shareholder` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 82(2) the last day for giving the notice` MEANS
    IF `the person was a substantial shareholder on 1 October 1971`
    THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` (Date 1 10 1971) 1 Months)   -- (a): "within one month after that date"
    ELSE IF `the day the person became a substantial shareholder` GREATER THAN (Date 1 10 1971)
         THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a number of business days after` `the day the person became a substantial shareholder` 2 `the public holidays`)   -- (b): "within 2 business days after becoming a substantial shareholder"
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the person was not a substantial shareholder on 1 October 1971 and did not become one after that date

@ref s 82(2) (src:9975-9982)
GIVEN `the person was a substantial shareholder on 1 October 1971` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person became a substantial shareholder` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82(2) the notice was given within the time the subsection allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 82(2) the last day for giving the notice` `the person was a substantial shareholder on 1 October 1971` `the day the person became a substantial shareholder` `the public holidays`
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        (IF `the day the notice was given` AT MOST lastDay
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must be given ... within 2 business days after becoming a substantial shareholder" -- a period the text fixes in its own words; outside it the answer is the text's no (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): see `s 82(2) the last day for giving the notice`

-- s 82(1) and (2)(b) as a regulative rule. The trace clock counts business days after the day the person became a substantial shareholder.
-- src:9966 | 82.—(1) A person who is a substantial shareholder in a company
-- src:9967 | must give written notice to the company stating the person’s name
-- src:9968 | and address and full particulars (including, unless the interest or
-- src:9969 | interests cannot be related to a particular share or shares, the name of
-- src:9970 | the person who is registered as the holder) of the voting shares in the
-- src:9971 | company in which the person has an interest or interests and full
-- src:9972 | particulars of each such interest and of the circumstances by reason of
-- src:9973 | which the person has that interest.
@ref s 82(1) (src:9966-9973)
GIVEN `the name of the person` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 82 act`
`s 82(1) a substantial shareholder must give notice to the company within 2 business days` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the person`
    MUST `s 82(1) give written notice to the company of the person's interests`
    WITHIN 2
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the person` BECAUSE "the substantial shareholder did not give the company written notice within 2 business days after becoming a substantial shareholder"

-- s 82(3): the notice must be given although the person has since ceased to be a substantial shareholder.
-- src:9984 | (3) The notice must be so given even though the person has ceased
-- src:9985 | to be a substantial shareholder before the expiration of whichever
-- src:9986 | period referred to in subsection (2) is applicable.
@ref s 82(3) (src:9984-9986)
GIVEN `the person ceased to be a substantial shareholder before the end of the period that applies under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 82(3) the notice must be given although the person has ceased to be a substantial shareholder` MEANS
    IF `the person ceased to be a substantial shareholder before the end of the period that applies under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The notice must be so given even though the person has ceased to be a substantial shareholder before the expiration of whichever period ... is applicable"; with no ceasing the subsection is silent and subsection (1) governs

§ `Section 83: substantial shareholder to notify company of change in interests`

DECLARE `s 83 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 83(1) give written notice to the company of the change in percentage level`

-- s 83(3): the percentage level: votes held as a percentage of the total votes (all voting shares, or all those of the class concerned), rounded down to a whole number.
-- src:10007 | (3) In subsection (1), “percentage level”, in relation to a substantial
-- src:10008 | shareholder, means the percentage figure ascertained by expressing
-- src:10013 | the total votes attached to all the voting shares in which the
-- src:10014 | substantial shareholder has an interest or interests immediately before
-- src:10015 | or (as the case may be) immediately after the relevant time as a
-- src:10016 | percentage of the total votes attached to —
-- src:10018 | (a) all the voting shares in the company; or
-- src:10020 | (b) where the share capital of the company is divided into 2 or
-- src:10021 | more classes of shares, all the voting shares included in the
-- src:10022 | class concerned,
-- src:10024 | and, if it is not a whole number, rounding that figure down to the next
-- src:10025 | whole number.
@ref s 83(3) (src:10007-10025)
GIVEN `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in which the substantial shareholder has an interest or interests` IS A NUMBER
      `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the company, or in the class concerned where the capital is divided into 2 or more classes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 83(3) the percentage level` MEANS
    IF `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the company, or in the class concerned where the capital is divided into 2 or more classes` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST (FLOOR ((`the total votes attached to all the voting shares in which the substantial shareholder has an interest or interests` TIMES 100) DIVIDED BY `the total votes attached to all the voting shares in the company, or in the class concerned where the capital is divided into 2 or more classes`))
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the subsection defines the level as a percentage of the total votes and says nothing where there are no votes

-- s 83(1): the duty arises where there is a change in the percentage level; notice within 2 business days after the substantial shareholder becomes aware.
-- src:9991 | 83.—(1) Where there is a change in the percentage level of the
-- src:9992 | interest or interests of a substantial shareholder in a company in
-- src:9993 | voting shares in the company, the substantial shareholder must give
-- src:9994 | written notice to the company stating the information specified in
-- src:9995 | subsection (2) within 2 business days after the substantial shareholder
-- src:9996 | becomes aware of such a change.
@ref s 83(1) (src:9991-9996)
GIVEN `the person is a substantial shareholder in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the percentage level immediately before the relevant time` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage level immediately after the relevant time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83(1) the substantial shareholder must give notice of a change in the percentage level` MEANS
    IF `the person is a substantial shareholder in the company` AND (NOT (`the percentage level immediately before the relevant time` EQUALS `the percentage level immediately after the relevant time`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where there is a change in the percentage level ... the substantial shareholder must give written notice" -- a duty whose "where" is unmet: the duty does not arise (fork F-j83-1, a duty whose "where" is unmet)

@ref s 83(1) (src:9991-9996)
GIVEN `the day the substantial shareholder becomes aware of the change` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 83(1) the last day for giving the notice` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a number of business days after` `the day the substantial shareholder becomes aware of the change` 2 `the public holidays`

@ref s 83(1) (src:9991-9996)
GIVEN `the day the substantial shareholder becomes aware of the change` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83(1) the notice was given within 2 business days after the substantial shareholder became aware` MEANS
    IF `the day the notice was given` AT MOST (`s 83(1) the last day for giving the notice` `the day the substantial shareholder becomes aware of the change` `the public holidays`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 2 business days after the substantial shareholder becomes aware of such a change" -- a period the text fixes in its own words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

@ref s 83(1) (src:9991-9996)
GIVEN `the name of the substantial shareholder` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 83 act`
`s 83(1) a substantial shareholder must give notice of a change within 2 business days` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the substantial shareholder`
    MUST `s 83(1) give written notice to the company of the change in percentage level`
    WITHIN 2
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the substantial shareholder` BECAUSE "the substantial shareholder did not give the company written notice of the change within 2 business days after becoming aware of it"

-- s 83(2): the information the notice states. Paragraph (c), "such other particulars as may be prescribed", is taken as a fact about the prescribed particulars.
-- src:9998 | (2) The information referred to in subsection (1) is —
-- src:10000 | (a) the name and address of the substantial shareholder;
-- src:10002 | (b) the date of the change and the circumstances leading to that
