      `the notice states the date of the change and the circumstances leading to that change` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states every other particular that is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 83(2) the notice states the information the subsection specifies` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the name and address of the substantial shareholder` AND `the notice states the date of the change and the circumstances leading to that change` AND `the notice states every other particular that is prescribed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must give written notice to the company stating the information specified in subsection (2)" -- a duty: the provision's own question

