      `the person holds the shares as the registered holder of the company's shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86(2A) section 86 applies to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Depository` AND `the person holds the shares as the registered holder of the company's shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to the Depository as the registered holder of a company’s shares"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says nothing of any other holder; subsection (1) governs

-- s 86(1): a holder of voting shares in which a non-resident has an interest must give the non-resident a notice in the prescribed form.
-- src:10056 | 86.—(1) A person who holds voting shares in a company, being
-- src:10057 | voting shares in which a non‑resident has an interest, must give to the
-- src:10062 | non‑resident a notice in the prescribed form as to the requirements of
-- src:10063 | this Division.
