      `a non-resident has an interest in those voting shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 86 applies to the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86(1) the holder must give the non-resident a notice` MEANS
    IF    `the person holds voting shares in a company`
      AND `a non-resident has an interest in those voting shares`
      AND (NOT (`section 86 applies to the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person who holds voting shares in a company, being voting shares in which a non-resident has an interest, must give to the non-resident a notice" -- a duty: the provision's own question (and s 86(2A) takes the Depository out)

@ref s 86(1) (src:10056-10063)
