      `the notice is as to the requirements of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86(1) the notice is the notice the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice is in the prescribed form` AND `the notice is as to the requirements of this Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must give to the non-resident a notice in the prescribed form as to the requirements of this Division" -- a duty: the provision's own question

-- s 86(2): when the notice must be given (calendar days).
-- src:10065 | (2) The notice must be given —
-- src:10067 | (a) if the firstmentioned person holds the shares on 1 October
-- src:10068 | 1971 — within 14 days after that date; or
-- src:10070 | (b) if the firstmentioned person did not hold the shares on that
