GIVEN `the person held the shares on 1 October 1971` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the person became the holder of the shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 86(2) the last day for giving the notice` MEANS
    IF `the person held the shares on 1 October 1971`
    THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` (Date 1 10 1971) 14 Days)   -- (a): "within 14 days after that date"
    ELSE IF `the day the person became the holder of the shares` GREATER THAN (Date 1 10 1971)
         THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the person became the holder of the shares` 2 Days)   -- (b): "within 2 days after becoming the holder of the shares"
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the person neither held the shares on 1 October 1971 nor became the holder after it

