    CONSIDER `s 86(2) the last day for giving the notice` `the person held the shares on 1 October 1971` `the day the person became the holder of the shares`
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        (IF `the day the notice was given` AT MOST lastDay
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 2 days after becoming the holder" -- a period the text fixes in its own words
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): see `s 86(2) the last day for giving the notice`

-- s 86(1) and (2)(b) as a regulative rule. The trace clock counts calendar days after the person became the holder.
