GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 88(5) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 88(5) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 88` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    --                          fine, months, both, default penalty
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

@ref s 88(5) (src:10127-10131)
GIVEN `the offence is a continuing offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of days the offence continues after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 88(5) the further fine for a continuing offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence is a continuing offence`
    THEN JUST (500 TIMES `the number of days the offence continues after conviction`)   -- "a further fine of $500 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the further fine is "in the case of a continuing offence"

-- s 88(6): nothing done under this Division gives the company notice of, or puts it on inquiry as to, a right in a share.
