GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88(6)(a) the company is to be taken to have notice of a right of a person to or in relation to a share` MEANS
    IF `the only ground is something done under this Division`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is not, by reason of anything done under this Division — (a) to be taken for any purpose to have notice of ... a right"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text speaks only of "anything done under this Division"

@ref s 88(6) (src:10133-10140)
GIVEN `the only ground is something done under this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 88(6)(b) the company is to be put upon inquiry as to a right of a person to or in relation to a share` MEANS
    IF `the only ground is something done under this Division`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company is not, by reason of anything done under this Division — (b) to be put upon inquiry as to ... a right"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text speaks only of "anything done under this Division"

