§ `Section 90: defence to prosecutions`

-- s 90(2): when a person is conclusively presumed to have been aware of a fact or occurrence.
-- src:10168 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), a person is conclusively
-- src:10169 | presumed to have been aware of a fact or occurrence at a particular
-- src:10170 | time —
-- src:10172 | (a) of which the person would, if the person had acted with
-- src:10173 | reasonable diligence in the conduct of the person’s affairs,
-- src:10174 | have been aware at that time; or
-- src:10176 | (b) of which an employee or agent of the person, being an
-- src:10177 | employee or agent having duties or acting in relation to his
-- src:10178 | or her master’s or principal’s interest or interests in a share
-- src:10179 | or shares in the company concerned, was aware or would,
-- src:10180 | if he or she had acted with reasonable diligence in the
-- src:10181 | conduct of his or her master’s or principal’s affairs, have
-- src:10182 | been aware at that time.
@ref s 90(2) (src:10168-10182)
GIVEN `the person would, had the person acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of the person's affairs, have been aware of it at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an employee or agent of the person, having duties or acting in relation to the person's interests in shares in the company, was aware of it at that time or would, had the employee or agent acted with reasonable diligence, have been aware of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90(2) the person is conclusively presumed to have been aware of the fact or occurrence at that time` MEANS
    IF    `the person would, had the person acted with reasonable diligence in the conduct of the person's affairs, have been aware of it at that time`
       OR `an employee or agent of the person, having duties or acting in relation to the person's interests in shares in the company, was aware of it at that time or would, had the employee or agent acted with reasonable diligence, have been aware of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "is conclusively presumed ... (a) ...; or (b) ..." does not say "only"; with neither limb the subsection is silent

-- s 90(1): the defence of not being aware. "less than 7 days before the date of the summons" is the number of days from the day the defendant became aware to the summons being under 7.
-- src:10152 | 90.—(1) It is a defence to a prosecution for failing to comply with
-- src:10153 | section 82, 83, 84 or 86 if the defendant proves that the defendant’s
-- src:10154 | failure was due to the defendant not being aware of a fact or
-- src:10159 | occurrence the existence of which was necessary to constitute the
-- src:10160 | offence and that —
-- src:10162 | (a) the defendant was not so aware on the date of the
-- src:10163 | summons; or
-- src:10165 | (b) the defendant became so aware less than 7 days before the
-- src:10166 | date of the summons.
@ref s 90(1) (src:10152-10166)
GIVEN `the prosecution is for failing to comply with section 82, 83, 84 or 86` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant proves that the failure was due to the defendant not being aware of a fact or occurrence the existence of which was necessary to constitute the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant is conclusively presumed under subsection (2) to have been aware` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the defendant was not so aware on the date of the summons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the defendant became so aware` IS A DATE
      `the date of the summons` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90(1) this section gives a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF    `the prosecution is for failing to comply with section 82, 83, 84 or 86`
      AND `the defendant proves that the failure was due to the defendant not being aware of a fact or occurrence the existence of which was necessary to constitute the offence`
      AND (NOT (`the defendant is conclusively presumed under subsection (2) to have been aware` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
      AND (   `the defendant was not so aware on the date of the summons`
           OR ((`the day the defendant became so aware` AT MOST `the date of the summons`) AND (NOT (`period: the date is at least a period before` `the day the defendant became so aware` `the date of the summons` 7 Days))))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence ... if the defendant proves that ..." -- when it is not proved this section gives no defence on these facts (ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b)); it does not say the defendant has no defence at all

§ `Section 91: powers of Court with respect to defaulting substantial shareholders`

DECLARE `s 91(1) order` IS ONE OF
    `s 91(1)(a) an order restraining the person from disposing of any interest in shares in the company`
    `s 91(1)(b) an order restraining a person who is, or is entitled to be registered as, the holder of those shares from disposing of any interest in them`
    `s 91(1)(c) an order restraining the exercise of any voting or other rights attached to any share`
    `s 91(1)(d) an order directing the company not to make payment, or to defer making payment, of any sum due in respect of a share`
    `s 91(1)(e) an order directing the sale of all or any of the shares`
    `s 91(1)(f) an order directing the company not to register the transfer or transmission of specified shares`
    `s 91(1)(g) an order that any exercise of the voting or other rights attached to specified shares be disregarded`
    `s 91(1)(h) an order, to secure compliance with another order, directing the company or any other person to do or refrain from doing a specified act`
    `s 91(1) another kind of order`

DECLARE `s 91 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 91(5) satisfy itself that the order would not unfairly prejudice any person`
    `s 91(6) make an order, other than an order restraining the exercise of voting rights, when it is satisfied that the failure was due to inadvertence, mistake or unawareness and ought to be excused`

-- s 91(1): "Where a person is a substantial shareholder, or at any time after 1 October 1971 has been a substantial shareholder in a company and has failed to comply with section 82, 83 or 84,
-- the Court may, on the application of the Minister, whether or not that failure still continues, make one or more of the following orders".
-- A function named for a power, gated by "where" and by the Minister's application: the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit (3): the answer is left as the periods ruling (b) gives it
-- ("where" fails: JUST FALSE) and the site is listed in the fork register for a lawyer (fork F-j91-1, split site (ii)).
-- src:10187 | 91.—(1) Where a person is a substantial shareholder, or at any time
-- src:10188 | after 1 October 1971 has been a substantial shareholder in a company
-- src:10189 | and has failed to comply with section 82, 83 or 84, the Court may, on
-- src:10190 | the application of the Minister, whether or not that failure still
-- src:10191 | continues, make one or more of the following orders:
-- src:10193 | (a) an order restraining the person from disposing of any
-- src:10194 | interest in shares in the company in which the person is or
-- src:10195 | has been a substantial shareholder;
-- src:10197 | (b) an order restraining a person who is, or is entitled to be
-- src:10198 | registered as, the holder of shares referred to in
-- src:10199 | paragraph (a) from disposing of any interest in those
-- src:10200 | shares;
-- src:10205 | (c) an order restraining the exercise of any voting or other
-- src:10206 | rights attached to any share in the company in which the
-- src:10207 | substantial shareholder has or has had an interest;
-- src:10209 | (d) an order directing the company not to make payment, or to
-- src:10210 | defer making payment, of any sum due from the company
-- src:10211 | in respect of any share in which the substantial shareholder
-- src:10212 | has or has had an interest;
-- src:10214 | (e) an order directing the sale of all or any of the shares in the
-- src:10215 | company in which the substantial shareholder has or has
-- src:10216 | had an interest;
-- src:10218 | (f) an order directing the company not to register the transfer
-- src:10219 | or transmission of specified shares;
-- src:10221 | (g) an order that any exercise of the voting or other rights
-- src:10222 | attached to specified shares in the company in which the
-- src:10223 | substantial shareholder has or has had an interest be
-- src:10224 | disregarded;
-- src:10226 | (h) for the purposes of securing compliance with any other
-- src:10227 | order made under this section, an order directing the
-- src:10228 | company or any other person to do or refrain from doing a
-- src:10229 | specified act.
@ref s 91(1) (src:10187-10229)
GIVEN `the person is a substantial shareholder in the company, or at any time after 1 October 1971 has been one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has failed to comply with section 82, 83 or 84` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has applied to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS A `s 91(1) order`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(1) the Court may make the order on the Minister's application` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a substantial shareholder in the company, or at any time after 1 October 1971 has been one`
      AND `the person has failed to comply with section 82, 83 or 84`
      AND `the Minister has applied to the Court`
    THEN (CONSIDER order
          WHEN `s 91(1) another kind of order` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the eight orders are listed without "only"; another kind of order is not covered
          OTHERWISE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, by the periods ruling (b)): "Where a person is a substantial shareholder ... and has failed to comply with section 82, 83 or 84, the Court may, on the application of the Minister" -- a "may" gated by "where" (listed for a lawyer)

-- s 91(2): ancillary or consequential provisions as the Court thinks just.
-- src:10231 | (2) Any order made under this section may include such ancillary or
-- src:10232 | consequential provisions as the Court thinks just.
@ref s 91(2) (src:10231-10232)
GIVEN `the provision is ancillary or consequential to an order made under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks the provision just` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(2) the order may include the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision is ancillary or consequential to an order made under this section` AND `the Court thinks the provision just`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may include such ancillary or consequential provisions as the Court thinks just" (a grant limited by its own wording, fork F-j91-2)

-- s 91(3): an order directing the sale of a share may set the time, conditions, and a condition that the sale is not to a person who is or would become a substantial shareholder.
-- src:10234 | (3) An order made under this section directing the sale of a share
-- src:10235 | may provide that the sale must be made within such time and subject
-- src:10236 | to such conditions (if any) as the Court thinks fit, including, if the
-- src:10237 | Court thinks fit, a condition that the sale must not be made to a person
-- src:10238 | who is, or, as a result of the sale, would become a substantial
-- src:10239 | shareholder in the company.
@ref s 91(3) (src:10234-10239)
GIVEN `the order directs the sale of a share` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court thinks the time or the conditions fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(3) the sale order may provide the time and conditions of the sale` MEANS
    IF `the order directs the sale of a share` AND `the Court thinks the time or the conditions fit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may provide that the sale must be made within such time and subject to such conditions (if any) as the Court thinks fit" (a grant limited by its own wording, fork F-j91-2)

-- s 91(4): the Court may direct that, where a share is not sold in accordance with an order, the share vests in the Registrar.
-- A "may" gated by "where": answered as the periods ruling (b) gives it (fork F-j91-1, split site (ii)).
-- src:10241 | (4) The Court may direct that, where a share is not sold in
-- src:10242 | accordance with an order of the Court under this section, the share
-- src:10243 | vests in the Registrar.
@ref s 91(4) (src:10241-10243)
GIVEN `the share has not been sold in accordance with an order of the Court under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(4) the Court may direct that the share vests in the Registrar` MEANS
    IF `the share has not been sold in accordance with an order of the Court under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, by the periods ruling (b)): "The Court may direct that, where a share is not sold in accordance with an order of the Court under this section, the share vests in the Registrar" -- a "may" gated by "where" (listed for a lawyer)

-- s 91(5): the Court must satisfy itself, before making an order and in determining its terms, that it would not unfairly prejudice any person.
-- src:10245 | (5) The Court must, before making an order under this section and
-- src:10246 | in determining the terms of such an order, satisfy itself, so far as it can
-- src:10251 | reasonably do so, that the order would not unfairly prejudice any
-- src:10252 | person.
@ref s 91(5) (src:10245-10252)
GIVEN `the Court is about to make an order under this section or to determine its terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(5) the Court must satisfy itself that the order would not unfairly prejudice any person` MEANS
    IF `the Court is about to make an order under this section or to determine its terms`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the duty is "before making an order under this section and in determining the terms of such an order"

-- The Court's duty as a regulative rule. No time limit and no consequence: no trace can show it breached (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 91(5) (src:10245-10252)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 91 act`
`s 91(5) the Court must satisfy itself before making an order` MEANS
    PARTY Court
    MUST `s 91(5) satisfy itself that the order would not unfairly prejudice any person`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: no deadline is modelled for this duty; dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Court BECAUSE "the Court made an order under this section without satisfying itself, so far as it could reasonably do so, that the order would not unfairly prejudice any person" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- s 91(6): the bar. "other than an order restraining the exercise of voting rights" is the carve-out in the text's own words; the bar applies if the Court is satisfied of (a) and (b).
-- Where the Court is not so satisfied the subsection is silent (the prohibition is limited by its own wording; marginal reading (b)).
-- src:10254 | (6) The Court must not make an order under this section, other than
-- src:10255 | an order restraining the exercise of voting rights, if it is satisfied —
-- src:10257 | (a) that the failure of the substantial shareholder to comply as
-- src:10258 | mentioned in subsection (1) was due to the substantial
-- src:10259 | shareholder’s inadvertence or mistake or to the substantial
-- src:10260 | shareholder not being aware of a relevant fact or
-- src:10261 | occurrence; and
-- src:10263 | (b) that in all the circumstances, the failure ought to be
-- src:10264 | excused.
@ref s 91(6) (src:10254-10264)
GIVEN `the order is an order restraining the exercise of voting rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that the failure was due to the substantial shareholder's inadvertence or mistake or to the substantial shareholder not being aware of a relevant fact or occurrence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court is satisfied that in all the circumstances the failure ought to be excused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91(6) the Court is barred from making the order` MEANS
    IF `the order is an order restraining the exercise of voting rights`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Court must not make an order under this section, other than an order restraining the exercise of voting rights" -- the carve-out: the bar does not apply to that order
    ELSE IF `the Court is satisfied that the failure was due to the substantial shareholder's inadvertence or mistake or to the substantial shareholder not being aware of a relevant fact or occurrence` AND `the Court is satisfied that in all the circumstances the failure ought to be excused`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must not make an order ... if it is satisfied (a) ... and (b) ..." -- a prohibition limited by its own wording; where the Court is not so satisfied the subsection does not say the Court may make the order

-- The prohibition as a regulative rule: the Court makes such an order. The act is BREACH; with no events the prohibition stands (RESIDUAL).
@ref s 91(6) (src:10254-10264)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 91 act`
`s 91(6) the Court must not make an order when it is satisfied that the failure ought to be excused` MEANS
    PARTY Court
    SHANT `s 91(6) make an order, other than an order restraining the exercise of voting rights, when it is satisfied that the failure was due to inadvertence, mistake or unawareness and ought to be excused`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Court BECAUSE "the Court made an order, other than an order restraining the exercise of voting rights, when it was satisfied that the failure was due to inadvertence, mistake or unawareness and ought to be excused"

